.TH INSTALL.SH 1 "2026-10-29" "mu2edaq-cluster-tools 1.0.1" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
install.sh \- per-user install of ssh\-selector and lan\-scan with launchers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./install.sh
.RB [ \-\-prefix
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-bin\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-app\-cmd
.IR NAME ]
.br
.B ./install.sh \-\-uninstall
.RB [ \-\-prefix
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B ./install.sh
.BR \-\-version | \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Finds the first of
.BR python3 ,
.BR python3.12 ,
.BR python3.11 ,
.BR python3.10 ,
.BR python3.9 ,
.B python
on
.B PATH
that is 3.9 or newer; creates or updates a venv in
.IR DIR/venv ;
installs this checkout into it; copies the topology files
.IR mu2e_daq.yaml ,
.IR mu2e_offline.yaml ,
.I nova_daq.yaml
and
.IR fnal_gpvm.yaml ,
plus the annotated
.IR hosts.yaml.example ,
into
.IR DIR/config/ ;
and writes two launcher scripts,
.I NAME
(default
.BR ssh\-selector )
and
.BR lan\-scan ,
into the bin directory.
.B lan\-scan
profiles are not installed as host files.
.PP
The installed
.BR ssh\-selector (1)
finds
.I DIR/config/*.yaml
as its last discovery tier, so it runs from any directory without
.BR \-c .
Personal host files go in
.IR ~/.config/mu2edaq/cluster\-tools/ ,
which is searched first after the current directory.
.SS Ownership and safety
Before anything is created the script writes a manifest,
.IR DIR/.mu2edaq\-cluster\-tools\-install ,
listing every path it will create: one
.RI \(dq kind \(rs t path \(dq
line per entry, kinds
.BR venv ,
.B file
and
.BR launcher .
.B \-\-uninstall
removes only what that manifest lists, and only if
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
a
.B venv
entry is exactly
.IR DIR/venv ;
.IP \(bu 2
a
.B file
entry lies strictly inside
.I DIR
and contains no
.IR .. ;
.IP \(bu 2
a
.B launcher
entry is a regular file carrying the
.B install.sh
generator tag and
.B exec\-ing
.IR DIR/venv/bin/ .
.RE
.PP
Then the manifest is removed,
.I DIR/config
and
.I DIR
are removed with
.BR rmdir (1)
if empty, and anything else is left in place with a warning.
A directory without the manifest is never touched.
.PP
Install and uninstall both refuse an empty
.IR DIR ,
.IR / ,
.BR $HOME ,
a small list of system directories, a path containing
.I ..
and a path containing a quote, dollar sign, backtick, backslash, tab or
newline (the path is embedded in the launchers).
Install refuses a non-empty
.I DIR
without the manifest, unless it holds exactly what
.B install.sh
1.0.1 and earlier created
.RI ( venv/
with an
.B ssh\-selector
entry point and
.IR config/hosts.yaml.example ),
which is adopted.
It refuses to overwrite a launcher that it did not write for the same
.IR DIR .
Re-running the install updates the venv and configs in place and keeps
launchers recorded by an earlier run (for example with another
.BR \-\-bin\-dir )
in the manifest.
.SH OPTIONS
Options override the matching environment variables, which override the
defaults.
Unknown options are an error (exit 2).
.TP
.BR \-\-prefix " \fIDIR\fR, " \-\-install\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Install directory.
Default
.IR ~/.local/share/mu2edaq\-cluster\-tools .
A relative path is taken relative to the current directory; a leading
.I ~
is expanded.
.TP
.BI \-\-bin\-dir " DIR"
Launcher directory, created if needed.
Default: the first existing of
.I ~/.local/bin
and
.IR ~/bin ,
else
.I ~/.local/bin
(created).
Ignored by
.BR \-\-uninstall ,
which uses the launcher paths in the manifest.
.TP
.BI \-\-app\-cmd " NAME"
Name of the
.B ssh\-selector
launcher.
Letters, digits,
.BR . ,
.B _
and
.B \-
only.
Default
.BR ssh\-selector .
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
Remove what the manifest in
.I DIR
lists, as described above.
No confirmation; the manifest is the guard.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print
.B mu2edaq\-cluster\-tools
.I version
(from
.IR src/mu2edaq_cluster_tools/_version.py )
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_CLUSTER_TOOLS_INSTALL_DIR
Install directory, overridden by
.BR \-\-prefix .
Also read by
.BR ssh\-selector (1)
for its install-directory discovery tier.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_CLUSTER_TOOLS_BIN_DIR
Launcher directory, overridden by
.BR \-\-bin\-dir .
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_CLUSTER_TOOLS_APP_CMD
Launcher name, overridden by
.BR \-\-app\-cmd .
.TP
.BR INSTALL_DIR ", " APP_CMD
Read by
.B install.sh
1.0.1 and earlier.
Now ignored, with a warning when set: the names are generic enough that
build environments export them for their own purposes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I DIR/.mu2edaq\-cluster\-tools\-install
Install manifest; marks
.I DIR
as created by this script.
.TP
.I DIR/venv/
Private virtual environment.
.TP
.I DIR/config/*.yaml
Topology files, discovered by
.BR ssh\-selector .
.TP
.I DIR/config/hosts.yaml.example
Annotated example.
.TP
.IR BIN/ssh\-selector ", " BIN/lan\-scan
Launchers that
.B exec
the venv's entry points.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including an uninstall that found no
.IR DIR .
.TP
.B 1
No Python 3.9+, an unsafe or foreign
.IR DIR ,
a foreign launcher in the way, a missing manifest on uninstall, or any
failing step
.RB ( "set \-e" ).
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option or missing option argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
\&./install.sh
ssh\-selector                         # finds DIR/config/*.yaml
\&./install.sh \-\-prefix /opt/mu2e/cluster\-tools \-\-bin\-dir /opt/mu2e/bin
\&./install.sh \-\-uninstall \-\-prefix /opt/mu2e/cluster\-tools
MU2EDAQ_CLUSTER_TOOLS_INSTALL_DIR=/tmp/ct ./install.sh \-\-bin\-dir /tmp/ct\-bin
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bootstrap.sh (1),
.BR ssh\-selector (1),
.BR lan\-scan (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
